<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/14th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tokhtamysh–Timur war</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1386–1395</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokhtamysh">Tokhtamysh</a>–<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timur">Timur</a> war was fought from 1386 to 1395 between Tokhtamysh, khan of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-horde">Golden Horde</a>, and his former patron Timur. Tokhtamysh raided Timur's lands in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transoxiana">Transoxiana</a>, but Timur defeated him at the Kondurcha River (1391) and the Terek (1395) and then sacked the Horde's cities, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sarai">Sarai</a>, a blow from which the Golden Horde never fully recovered.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tokhtamysh-timur-war.jpg" alt="Tokhtamysh–Timur war" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 15th-century artist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_between_Timur_and_Toqtamish_Khan,_1420-1440,_possibly_Herat._Topkapi_H.2153.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
